{"cuisine/peruvian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/peruvian-cuisine","n":"Peruvian cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Peru","intro":[["Peruvian cuisine refers to the culinary and gastronomical traditions of Peru, which originated in the pre-Columbian indigenous populations in its three main geographical regions along the Pacific coast, the Andes and the Amazonian areas. Some of the fare blends traditions that came after the arrival of the Spaniards in the 1530s, with immigrants from Europe (Spanish cuisine, Italian cuisine, and German cuisine), Asia (Chinese cuisine and Japanese cuisine), the Middle East, and Africa (Maghrebi cuisine and West African cuisine). Lacking ingredients often available in their original countries, these immigrants blended their recipes with those locally available in Peru."],["The four traditional staples of Peruvian cuisine are corn; potatoes and other tubers; Amaranthaceae (quinoa, kañiwa and kiwicha); and legumes (beans and lupins). Staples brought by the Spanish include rice, wheat and meats (beef, pork and chicken)."],["Many traditional foods—such as quinoa, kiwicha, chili peppers, and several roots and tubers—have increased in popularity in recent decades, reflecting a revival of interest in native Peruvian foods and culinary techniques. Chef Gastón Acurio has become well known for raising awareness of local ingredients. The most important ingredient in Peruvian cuisine is the potato, as Peru has the widest variety of potatoes in the world."],["American food critic Eric Asimov has described it as one of the world's most important cuisines and an exemplar of fusion cuisine, due to its long multicultural history."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"peruvian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peruvian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Peru Delights","ref":"site/perudelights-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"perudelights.com","note":"Morena Cuadra's blog of Peruvian home recipes and food culture.","url":"https://perudelights.com/tag/peruvian-home-cooking/","suggested":true},{"name":"Eat Peru","ref":"site/eatperu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"eatperu.com","note":"Guide to Peruvian dishes and ingredients with a recipe section.","url":"https://www.eatperu.com/category/recipes/?sf_paged=2","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Peru: The Cookbook","ref":"cookbook/peru-the-cookbook","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Gastón Acurio, 2015","note":"Large collection of Peruvian home recipes from Peru's best-known chef.","url":"https://www.phaidon.com/en-us/products/peru-the-cookbook/","suggested":true},{"name":"The Fire of Peru","ref":"cookbook/the-fire-of-peru","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Ricardo Zarate","note":"Peruvian dishes adapted for home kitchens by a Lima-born chef working in the US.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27190726M/The_fire_of_Peru","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":13,"links":[["Andina (restaurant)","dish/andina-restaurant"],["Anticucho","dish/anticucho"],["Central (restaurant)","dish/central-restaurant"],["Chicha morada","dish/chicha-morada"],["Coca tea","dish/coca-tea"],["La Rosa Náutica","dish/la-rosa-nautica"],["Lima (restaurant)","dish/lima-restaurant"],["Locro","dish/locro"],["Maido (restaurant)","dish/maido-restaurant"],["Peruvian ceviche","dish/peruvian-ceviche"],["Picantería","dish/picanteria"],["Picarones","dish/picarones"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Capsicum chinense","ingredient/capsicum-chinense"],["Offal","ingredient/offal"],["Purple corn","ingredient/purple-corn"],["Coca leaf","ingredient/coca-leaf"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Beef jerky","ingredient/beef-jerky"],["Cayenne pepper","ingredient/cayenne-pepper"],["Chorizo","ingredient/chorizo"],["Hot sauce","ingredient/hot-sauce"],["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Paprika","ingredient/paprika"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Zapallo","ingredient/zapallo"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Chancaca","ingredient/chancaca"],["Cucurbita maxima","ingredient/cucurbita-maxima"],["Fig","ingredient/fig"],["Panela","ingredient/panela"],["Squash (plant)","ingredient/squash-plant"],["Sweet potato","ingredient/sweet-potato"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Bell pepper","ingredient/bell-pepper"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Within Peruvian cooking","count":5,"links":[["Amazonian cuisine","cuisine/amazonian-cuisine"],["Arequipan cuisine","cuisine/arequipan-cuisine"],["Inca cuisine","cuisine/inca-cuisine"],["Peruvian-Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chifa"],["Peruvian-Japanese cuisine","cuisine/nikkei-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Peru","count":1,"links":[["Quechua foodways","cuisine/quechua-foodways"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c2/Buffet_Costa_Verde.jpg/500px-Buffet_Costa_Verde.jpg","w":500,"h":890,"by":"MiguelAlanCS","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buffet_Costa_Verde.jpg"}},"cuisine/norwegian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/norwegian-cuisine","n":"Norwegian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Norway","intro":[["Norwegian cuisine in its traditional form is based largely on the raw materials readily available in Norway. It differs in many respects from continental cuisine with a stronger focus on game and fish. Many of the traditional dishes are the result of using conserved materials because of the long winters."],["Modern Norwegian cuisine, although still strongly influenced by its traditional background, has been influenced by globalization: pasta, spicebags, pizza, burgers, fries, soda, martinis, tacos, and the like are as common as meatballs and cod as staple foods."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"norwegian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norwegian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"North Wild Kitchen: Home Cooking from the Heart of Norway","ref":"cookbook/north-wild-kitchen-home-cooking-from-the-heart-of-norway","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Nevada Berg, 2018","note":"Traditional Norwegian home cooking from the author of the North Wild Kitchen blog, published by Prestel.","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/586680/north-wild-kitchen-by-nevada-berg/9783791384139/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":12,"links":[["Ekebergrestauranten","dish/ekebergrestauranten"],["Engebret Café","dish/engebret-cafe"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Fruktsoppa","dish/fruktsoppa"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Kransekage","dish/kransekage"],["Labskaus","dish/labskaus"],["Lutefisk","dish/lutefisk"],["Restaurant Schrøder","dish/restaurant-schr-der"],["Risalamande","dish/risalamande"],["Stortorvets Gjæstgiveri","dish/stortorvets-gj-stgiveri"],["Trollkrem","dish/trollkrem"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Atlantic cod","ingredient/atlantic-cod"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["French fries","ingredient/french-fries"],["Fried fish","ingredient/fried-fish"],["Fries","ingredient/fries"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Dried fruit","ingredient/dried-fruit"],["Red wine","ingredient/red-wine"],["Mulled wine","ingredient/mulled-wine"],["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Wine","ingredient/wine"],["Egg white","ingredient/egg-white"],["Prunus dulcis","ingredient/prunus-dulcis"],["Corned beef","ingredient/corned-beef"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Potatoes","ingredient/potatoes"],["Salted meat","ingredient/salted-meat"],["Sodium hydroxide","ingredient/sodium-hydroxide"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Rice pudding","ingredient/rice-pudding"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/26/Norwegian.cuisine-Reinsdyrsteik-01.jpg/500px-Norwegian.cuisine-Reinsdyrsteik-01.jpg","w":500,"h":628,"by":"by tuey","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Norwegian.cuisine-Reinsdyrsteik-01.jpg"}},"dish/ayran":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ayran","n":"Ayran","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Balkan cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Ayran ( eye-RAHN, also ayryan) is a cold savory yogurt-based beverage found throughout Central Asia, the Balkans, and the Middle East. The drink is a heterogeneous mixture that has been consumed by Turkic peoples for approximately 1,000 years. The principal ingredients are yogurt, water and salt. Herbs such as mint may be added, and some varieties are carbonated. It is a national drink of Turkey and is served in most restaurants in Bulgaria."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ayran"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayran"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Balkan cuisine","cuisine/balkan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"]]},{"h":"More from Balkan cuisine","links":[["Ajvar","dish/ajvar"],["Stuffed tomatoes","dish/stuffed-tomatoes"],["Tarator","dish/tarator"],["Torshi","dish/torshi"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/8/8e/Fresh_ayran.jpg","w":500,"h":674,"by":"Mavigogun","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fresh_ayran.jpg"}},"ingredient/machaca":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/machaca","n":"Machaca","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Machaca is a traditionally dried meat, usually spiced beef or pork, that is rehydrated and then used in popular local cuisine in Northern Mexico and the Southwestern United States.  It is also readily available in many groceries and supermarkets in these areas. In areas where the dried meat product is not easy to obtain, slow-cooked roast beef (brisket) or skirt steak shredded and then fried is sometimes substituted."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-machaca"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machaca"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"]]],["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",[["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Adobada","ingredient/adobada"],["Bean","ingredient/bean"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Flour tortilla","ingredient/flour-tortilla"],["Jalapeño","ingredient/jalapeno"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Tortilla","ingredient/tortilla"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/45/Machaca_%2832157311937%29.jpg/500px-Machaca_%2832157311937%29.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Dale Cruse from San Francisco, CA, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Machaca_(32157311937).jpg"}},"dish/doujiang":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/doujiang","n":"Doujiang","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Doujiang is fresh soy milk in Chinese cuisine. It can be served hot or cool, sweet or savoury. Sometimes, it is lightly curdled with vinegar. It is a common breakfast item served with youtiao."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-doujiang"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doujiang"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"],["Taiwan cuisine","cuisine/taiwan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Soybean","ingredient/soybean"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","ref":"site/youtube-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true},{"name":"Red House Spice","ref":"site/redhousespice-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Cooking in Chinglish","ref":"site/cookinginchinglish-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookinginchinglish.com","note":"Taiwanese home recipes from Edwina, who grew up in Taiwan.","url":"https://cookinginchinglish.com","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["A+ Hong Kong Kitchen","dish/a-hong-kong-kitchen"],["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Chinese Tuxedo","dish/chinese-tuxedo"],["Chowking","dish/chowking"],["Classic Savory","dish/classic-savory"],["Country Dough","dish/country-dough"],["Cuisine AuntDai","dish/cuisine-auntdai"],["Dandan noodles","dish/dandan-noodles"],["Dapanji","dish/dapanji"],["Dim Sum King","dish/dim-sum-king"],["Dong'an chicken","dish/dong-an-chicken"],["Dongpo pork","dish/dongpo-pork"],["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"],["Drunken shrimp","dish/drunken-shrimp"],["Duck House Chinese Restaurant","dish/duck-house-chinese-restaurant"],["Edible bird's nest","dish/edible-bird-s-nest"],["Fish sauce","dish/fish-sauce"],["Flower Drum","dish/flower-drum"],["Frank Fat's","dish/frank-fat-s"],["Fuqi feipian","dish/fuqi-feipian"],["Gaifan","dish/gaifan"],["Goubuli","dish/goubuli"],["Hainanese chicken rice","dish/hainanese-chicken-rice"],["Handpulled Noodle","dish/handpulled-noodle"],["Harbor City Restaurant","dish/harbor-city-restaurant"],["Heichinrou","dish/heichinrou"],["HK Cafe","dish/hk-cafe"],["Hog maw","dish/hog-maw"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"],["Hot pot","dish/hot-pot"],["Hotcha (company)","dish/hotcha-company"],["House of Louie","dish/house-of-louie"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/1e/Doujiang_and_youtiao_Taipei.jpg/500px-Doujiang_and_youtiao_Taipei.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"KQuhen","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doujiang_and_youtiao_Taipei.jpg"}},"dish/fartura":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/fartura","n":"Fartura","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Portuguese cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["A fartura is a fried dough made of flour, yeast, baking soda, salt, sugar, cinnamon, and water, that is fried in oil, in the form of a roll and traditionally sold at fairs in Portugal. It is preferable to consume them when they are hot so that the crunchy surface does not harden."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-fartura"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fartura"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Food From Portugal","ref":"site/foodfromportugal-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"foodfromportugal.com","note":"Portuguese-run recipe site and video channel of traditional Portuguese dishes.","url":"https://www.foodfromportugal.com/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Portuguese cuisine","links":[["Adega","dish/adega"],["Alheira","dish/alheira"],["Amêijoas à Bulhão Pato","dish/ameijoas-a-bulhao-pato"],["Arroz de marisco","dish/arroz-de-marisco"],["Bacalhau à Brás","dish/bacalhau-a-bras"],["Bacalhau à Gomes de Sá","dish/bacalhau-a-gomes-de-sa"],["Bacalhau à minhota","dish/bacalhau-a-minhota"],["Bacalhau à Narcisa","dish/bacalhau-a-narcisa"],["Bacalhau à Zé do Pipo","dish/bacalhau-a-ze-do-pipo"],["Bacalhau com natas","dish/bacalhau-com-natas"],["Batatas a murro","dish/batatas-a-murro"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bolo de bolacha","dish/bolo-de-bolacha"],["Canja de galinha","dish/canja-de-galinha"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Encharcada","dish/encharcada"],["Feijoada","dish/feijoada"],["Fios de ovos","dish/fios-de-ovos"],["Francesinha","dish/francesinha"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Pão Alentejano","dish/pao-alentejano"],["Pão de Ló","dish/pao-de-lo"],["Pataniscas","dish/pataniscas"],["Polvo à lagareiro","dish/polvo-a-lagareiro"],["Prego (Portuguese sandwich)","dish/prego-portuguese-sandwich"],["Pudim Abade de Priscos","dish/pudim-abade-de-priscos"],["Pudim Molotov","dish/pudim-molotov"],["Sericaia","dish/sericaia"],["Serradura","dish/serradura"],["Tocino de cielo","dish/tocino-de-cielo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c3/Farturas_2010_17_%28RaBoe%29.jpg/500px-Farturas_2010_17_%28RaBoe%29.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"© Ra Boe / Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Farturas_2010_17_(RaBoe).jpg"}},"dish/kig-ha-farz":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kig-ha-farz","n":"Kig ha farz","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Kig ha farz is a cooked dish consisting of various meats simmered in a broth with a buckwheat flour-based pudding. It is eaten traditionally in Brittany, more specifically around Léon in the region situated west from Morlaix to Brest. This dish, which is similar to a pot-au-feu, was once considered a dish for the poor and the peasantry.  The name in Breton literally means \"meat and stuffing\"."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kig-ha-farz"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kig_ha_farz"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Buckwheat","ingredient/buckwheat"],["Buckwheat flour","ingredient/buckwheat-flour"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Pudding","ingredient/pudding"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","ref":"site/newcaledonia-travel","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links":[["'t Fornuis","dish/t-fornuis"],["'t Misverstant","dish/t-misverstant"],["'t Vlasbloeme