creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nasi_Minyak_Palembang_1.jpg"}},"dish/paska-bread":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/paska-bread","n":"Paska (bread)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Paska is a traditional Ukrainian Easter bread particularly spread in Central and Eastern European countries with cultural connections to the ancient Byzantine Empire, Eastern Orthodoxy or Eastern Catholicism. Easter breads are a traditional element in the Easter holiday cuisines of Armenia, Belarus, Bulgaria, Croatia, Georgia, Moldova, Romania, Russia, Poland, Slovakia and Ukraine. It is also eaten in countries with large immigrant populations from Central and Eastern Europe such as the United States, Canada and the United Kingdom. Easter bread is also a common tradition amongst the Assyrian diaspora."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-paska-bread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paska_(bread)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine"],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","ref":"site/olgasflavorfactory-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true},{"name":"Savas Kitchen: Ukrainian recipes","ref":"site/savaskitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"savaskitchen.com","note":"Ukrainian-born home cook Nataliia Savas's section of family Ukrainian recipes.","url":"https://savaskitchen.com/category/ukrainian-recip